From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:16:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Answer that the buffer is too small for a token's
 privileges when their count does not fit.

A token without privileges needs no room for them but still four bytes for the count: asked with no
buffer, NtQueryInformationToken(TokenPrivileges) said it had succeeded, and with a buffer of one to
three bytes it wrote the count past it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/security.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/security.c
index cfde4587c29..12c80de5a46 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/security.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/security.c
@@ -478,7 +478,12 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtQueryInformationToken( HANDLE token, TOKEN_INFORMATION_CLASS c
                 wine_server_set_reply( req, tpriv->Privileges, length - FIELD_OFFSET( TOKEN_PRIVILEGES, Privileges ) );
             status = wine_server_call( req );
             if (retlen) *retlen = FIELD_OFFSET( TOKEN_PRIVILEGES, Privileges ) + reply->len;
-            if (tpriv) tpriv->PrivilegeCount = reply->len / sizeof(LUID_AND_ATTRIBUTES);
+            /* the count has to fit even when there is no privilege to list */
+            if (length < FIELD_OFFSET( TOKEN_PRIVILEGES, Privileges ))
+            {
+                if (!status) status = STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;
+            }
+            else if (tpriv) tpriv->PrivilegeCount = reply->len / sizeof(LUID_AND_ATTRIBUTES);
         }
         SERVER_END_REQ;
         break;
